
# ========== conditional_statement=========
  - a conditional statement in python  is used to make decisions.
  - the progrsm execute different blocks of code based on whether a conddtion is True or False.

# --------- there are---------
 - if statement
 - else statement
 - if-else statement
 - if-elif-else statement
 - nested-if statement
 - condition used comparision operators
 - condition used logical operators
 
# -------------- key points--------

if checks a condition,if it's True go inside  ,False it never execute
else runs when the condition is False.
elif checks additional conditions.
Python uses indentation (4 spaces) to define code blocks.
Conditions always evaluate to either True or False.
You can combine conditions using and, or, and not.

